The ORR activities of these electro-catalysts were tested in $\mathbf{O}_{2}$ -saturated $0.1\textbf{M}$ KOH electrolyte, and the activity data are shown in Figure 9. The onset potential (Eonset is the potential at the current density of - $-0.1\mathrm{mA}/\mathrm{cm}^{2}\mathrm{\Omega}$ ) is an important parameter to evaluate the performance of electrocatalyst. The ORR activities of PAN-800 and ZIF-67-800 are poor with an $\mathrm{E_{onset}}$ of $0.86\mathrm{~V~}$ and $0.87~\mathrm{V}$ and the half-wave potential $\left(\operatorname{E}_{1/2}\right)$ of $0.74\mathrm{V}$ and $0.80{\mathrm{V}}$ , respectively. Obviously, the ZIF-67/PAN-800 has an onset potential of $0.90{\mathrm{~V~}}$ and a half-wave potential $\left(\operatorname{E}_{1/2}\right)$ of $0.81~\mathrm{V}$ (slightly negative than 20 wt% Pt/C: 0.93 V and $0.82\mathrm{~V~}$ respectively), while PAN-800 and ZIF-67-800 display more negative onset potentials and $\mathrm{E}_{1/2}$ as mentioned above (Figure 9a and Table 3). These results suggest that the ZIF-67/PAN-800 has a higher ORR activity, which is comparable with that of $20\mathrm{\wt}\%$ Pt/C. In addition, ZIF-67/PAN-800 has the lowest Tafel slope $(49.5\mathrm{mV}$ dec-1) among that of PAN-800 ( $83.5\mathrm{mV}$ dec-1), ZIF-67-800 $(65.5\mathrm{mV\dec^{-1}}.$ ) and $20\mathrm{wt}\%$ Pt/C ( $62.5\mathrm{mV}$ dec-1) (Figure 9b and Table 3), which indicates ZIF-67/PAN-800 had a better performing ORR kinetic.
